Black (Linux native) - black-linux
==================================

An unofficial native Linux port of the original Xbox version of Black (2006),
made by static recompilation with XboxXBE-Recomp (TGP482), using the
game hooks, sound and Vulkan renderer of Black for Android (Rangga Casper).
No emulator, no Wine/Proton, no Electron, no web engine.

This package contains NO game code and NO game assets.

FIRST START
  1. Put YOUR OWN copy of the game (USA or Europe) in
         ~/.local/share/black-linux/game/
     either the disc image (.iso) or default.xbe with its folders.
     (Or just start the game: it asks you to pick the .iso.)
  2. Start "Black (Linux Native)" from the menu, or run:  black-linux
  3. The first start compiles the game for your PC: 30-90 minutes, once.
     In a terminal you can watch it:  black-linux-build

PLAYING
  F11 or Alt+Enter   fullscreen / window
  Esc / the game's   options: Graphics, Mouse and Keyboard, General ...
  black-linux --windowed     start in a window
  black-linux --rebuild      build again (e.g. after changing the game files)

FILES
  ~/.local/share/black-linux/          settings (black.toml), saves (hdd),
                                       logs, built game (bin/BLACK)
  ~/.cache/black-linux/build.log       the build's log

LOW-END LAPTOPS (Intel HD 520/620)
  Graphics > Render Resolution 67-100%, MSAA/SMAA off, Ambient Occlusion off,
  V-Sync on. Check Vulkan works:  vulkaninfo --summary

TROUBLESHOOTING
  - "compiling failed": low memory; run  black-linux-build --jobs 1
  - no picture / crash at start: sudo apt install mesa-vulkan-drivers, update
    Mesa, and see ~/.local/share/black-linux/logs
